{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[],"claim_ids":[],"created_at":"2026-09-14T03:15:54Z","created_by_operation":"op_0dc34ece6c474b6d84cb523f4888da66","id":"pg_2b4c6bb4defc5bafb812cb4db116cdc0","maturity":"draft","page_type":"source","path":"pages/sources/strategic-automation-dspy-compounding-engineering-pr-description-md-91-cb4db116cdc0.md","record_type":"page","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","source_ids":["src_9835c6e6da0b5ef8a34dfa6b2b0d4834"],"title":"Strategic-Automation/dspy-compounding-engineering/pr_description.md @ 918f63caff79","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:15:54Z","updated_by_operation":"op_0dc34ece6c474b6d84cb523f4888da66"}
{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[{"claim_ids":["clm_0c8b310c35c06e63bd9bf6b68601577f9b48d0c1eb1d6254282a1e323f5cdf14"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Installation is uv-based: a recommended installer script locks Python 3.12 in an isolated environment, a pip wrapper (dspyce-install) bootstraps uv, and a repo-root ./uvx wrapper runs the CLI without global install."},{"claim_ids":["clm_140ba188d741e515c5fe9659795b85555510f54b6f081df3d1b07095da9f815e"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Configuration is loaded in priority order: --env-file flag, COMPOUNDING_ENV variable, CWD .env, ~/.config/compounding/.env, then ~/.env, with a warning on conflicting files."},{"claim_ids":["clm_2282cc45b7b763672a60bffcde8e090ecb761c78a0c2ab299357fea5fffa4fcf"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The CLI also includes a generate-agent command that creates new review agents from a natural language description, with a --dry-run option."},{"claim_ids":["clm_519257e91ad178073e35be7c1f61147855fd64c14a0807f1df44f1037a86e518"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Work execution can run in isolated git worktrees for safe parallel execution, with automatic worktree cleanup after completion."},{"claim_ids":["clm_52a42e925f6d311e8f109073c74063fe67b141093ec1162576ee220543af3485"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The project depends on the DSPy framework, supports LLM providers OpenAI, Anthropic, Ollama, and OpenRouter via env config, and uses Playwright (Chromium) for documentation fetching."},{"claim_ids":["clm_579119dc01569c49d291fd01c2e675d95c545e0b2f991307cfbad0a2d6d457cc"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Global options include -e/--env-file and -h/--help; the work command supports --dry-run, --worktree, --sequential, and --workers flags."},{"claim_ids":["clm_8395cb28fc32919358425a6857a0e1a67d6b9631a8ac6d4ccce4557f5ce9ccf1"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The tool is designed as a local-first CLI running on the user's machine, in contrast to the original Claude Code plugin it reimplements."},{"claim_ids":["clm_99fffbc13297e97fe4adb725d74312a2ec89cb7a81525bd790a082beabb62262"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Repository development practice: contributors are directed to CONTRIBUTING.md for guidelines, and source setup involves cloning, copying .env.example to .env, and running 'uv sync'."},{"claim_ids":["clm_9b5a268f1b5137b90e378a75e14166d12d3a5879c1be6f60b8a9042f03054a22"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The tool can run as an MCP server (compounding-mcp, described as a FastMCP server) exposing compounding_review, compounding_plan, compounding_work, compounding_triage, and compounding_sync tools to clients like Claude Desktop."},{"claim_ids":["clm_a1fd99747b9dc8f7c8c2a6bef42a8fcab4b9077de626776b492f6d8b9fb6b9de"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The system is layered: a CLI layer (cli.py), orchestration layer (workflows/), DSPy agents layer (agents/), knowledge layer, and infrastructure/utils layer."},{"claim_ids":["clm_a4de5b450f2907fd55cee35dea117bd8351a943693a1b6ed772b3b22c912fbd3"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The product exposes a Typer-based CLI ('compounding') with commands including review, triage, work, plan, and codify, mapping user intents to workflows."},{"claim_ids":["clm_b3589ade229303d9d7034ba686bdb8cfa53d3dd97fd8a2eca8de042357c89a46"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Learnings are persisted as structured JSON in a .knowledge/ directory, with keyword/tag-based retrieval and automatic injection of relevant past learnings into agent calls via a KBPredict wrapper."},{"claim_ids":["clm_bd7a9278969d1cc51945dd59810d9610efe684f428320877088deafd35e6d2cd"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Qdrant is used for semantic search (startable via Docker Compose on localhost:6333); if Qdrant is not running, the system falls back to keyword-based search over local JSON files."},{"claim_ids":["clm_d8f3fe892b2a15961648c6a102734991a85ea0dc06ae0dadef85a09bcba711f4"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Parallelism uses ThreadPoolExecutor for multi-agent and multi-todo execution, with --workers to set worker count and --sequential for serial mode."},{"claim_ids":["clm_f286d75ec5e663819d15c0c6b19c35a71ad7ec3a4902f32a305dc039d06e8b42"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Review agents include specialized roles such as Security Sentinel (vulnerabilities), Performance Oracle (bottlenecks), Architecture Strategist, and Data Integrity Guardian, with 10+ agents run in parallel."}],"claim_ids":["clm_0c8b310c35c06e63bd9bf6b68601577f9b48d0c1eb1d6254282a1e323f5cdf14","clm_140ba188d741e515c5fe9659795b85555510f54b6f081df3d1b07095da9f815e","clm_2282cc45b7b763672a60bffcde8e090ecb761c78a0c2ab299357fea5fffa4fcf","clm_519257e91ad178073e35be7c1f61147855fd64c14a0807f1df44f1037a86e518","clm_52a42e925f6d311e8f109073c74063fe67b141093ec1162576ee220543af3485","clm_579119dc01569c49d291fd01c2e675d95c545e0b2f991307cfbad0a2d6d457cc","clm_8395cb28fc32919358425a6857a0e1a67d6b9631a8ac6d4ccce4557f5ce9ccf1","clm_99fffbc13297e97fe4adb725d74312a2ec89cb7a81525bd790a082beabb62262","clm_9b5a268f1b5137b90e378a75e14166d12d3a5879c1be6f60b8a9042f03054a22","clm_a1fd99747b9dc8f7c8c2a6bef42a8fcab4b9077de626776b492f6d8b9fb6b9de","clm_a4de5b450f2907fd55cee35dea117bd8351a943693a1b6ed772b3b22c912fbd3","clm_b3589ade229303d9d7034ba686bdb8cfa53d3dd97fd8a2eca8de042357c89a46","clm_bd7a9278969d1cc51945dd59810d9610efe684f428320877088deafd35e6d2cd","clm_d8f3fe892b2a15961648c6a102734991a85ea0dc06ae0dadef85a09bcba711f4","clm_f286d75ec5e663819d15c0c6b19c35a71ad7ec3a4902f32a305dc039d06e8b42"],"created_at":"2026-09-14T03:15:54Z","created_by_operation":"op_0dc34ece6c474b6d84cb523f4888da66","id":"pg_2e89e4999bde5c0fa9b74c3d2375827e","maturity":"draft","page_type":"source","path":"pages/sources/strategic-automation-dspy-compounding-engineering-readme-md-918f63caff-4c3d2375827e.md","record_type":"page","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","source_ids":["src_f0a7a9d0806c54ac814fe8ec356e813e"],"title":"Strategic-Automation/dspy-compounding-engineering/README.md @ 918f63caff79","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:15:54Z","updated_by_operation":"op_0dc34ece6c474b6d84cb523f4888da66"}
{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[{"claim_ids":["clm_519257e91ad178073e35be7c1f61147855fd64c14a0807f1df44f1037a86e518"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Work execution can run in isolated git worktrees for safe parallel execution, with automatic worktree cleanup after completion."},{"claim_ids":["clm_53ac4d4066fcc6c4e0a74f202afc9190610b6685358358742d7ec7395768d386"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Workflows orchestrate multi-step processes: the review pipeline parallelizes agents and writes pending todo files, triage interactively converts them to ready, and unified work executes them via ReAct loops, marking them complete."},{"claim_ids":["clm_a1fd99747b9dc8f7c8c2a6bef42a8fcab4b9077de626776b492f6d8b9fb6b9de"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The system is layered: a CLI layer (cli.py), orchestration layer (workflows/), DSPy agents layer (agents/), knowledge layer, and infrastructure/utils layer."},{"claim_ids":["clm_a4de5b450f2907fd55cee35dea117bd8351a943693a1b6ed772b3b22c912fbd3"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The product exposes a Typer-based CLI ('compounding') with commands including review, triage, work, plan, and codify, mapping user intents to workflows."},{"claim_ids":["clm_b3589ade229303d9d7034ba686bdb8cfa53d3dd97fd8a2eca8de042357c89a46"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Learnings are persisted as structured JSON in a .knowledge/ directory, with keyword/tag-based retrieval and automatic injection of relevant past learnings into agent calls via a KBPredict wrapper."},{"claim_ids":["clm_d8f3fe892b2a15961648c6a102734991a85ea0dc06ae0dadef85a09bcba711f4"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Parallelism uses ThreadPoolExecutor for multi-agent and multi-todo execution, with --workers to set worker count and --sequential for serial mode."},{"claim_ids":["clm_f286d75ec5e663819d15c0c6b19c35a71ad7ec3a4902f32a305dc039d06e8b42"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Review agents include specialized roles such as Security Sentinel (vulnerabilities), Performance Oracle (bottlenecks), Architecture Strategist, and Data Integrity Guardian, with 10+ agents run in parallel."}],"claim_ids":["clm_519257e91ad178073e35be7c1f61147855fd64c14a0807f1df44f1037a86e518","clm_53ac4d4066fcc6c4e0a74f202afc9190610b6685358358742d7ec7395768d386","clm_a1fd99747b9dc8f7c8c2a6bef42a8fcab4b9077de626776b492f6d8b9fb6b9de","clm_a4de5b450f2907fd55cee35dea117bd8351a943693a1b6ed772b3b22c912fbd3","clm_b3589ade229303d9d7034ba686bdb8cfa53d3dd97fd8a2eca8de042357c89a46","clm_d8f3fe892b2a15961648c6a102734991a85ea0dc06ae0dadef85a09bcba711f4","clm_f286d75ec5e663819d15c0c6b19c35a71ad7ec3a4902f32a305dc039d06e8b42"],"created_at":"2026-09-14T03:15:54Z","created_by_operation":"op_0dc34ece6c474b6d84cb523f4888da66","id":"pg_92ae95e7a31b57c7a7e05fdb30891ae4","maturity":"draft","page_type":"source","path":"pages/sources/strategic-automation-dspy-compounding-engineering-docs-concepts-archit-5fdb30891ae4.md","record_type":"page","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","source_ids":["src_232492dfccbf54a9be6fd1d1efc029ed"],"title":"Strategic-Automation/dspy-compounding-engineering/docs/concepts/architecture.md @ 918f63caff79","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:15:54Z","updated_by_operation":"op_0dc34ece6c474b6d84cb523f4888da66"}
{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[{"claim_ids":["clm_1d4e64be3035c748c818e5eb328fc24029a5ad988b2d3c15da08e98704e505d1"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"A sync command parses pending/ready todo markdown files and creates or updates GitHub issues, writing the issue URL back into todo frontmatter."},{"claim_ids":["clm_2282cc45b7b763672a60bffcde8e090ecb761c78a0c2ab299357fea5fffa4fcf"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The CLI also includes a generate-agent command that creates new review agents from a natural language description, with a --dry-run option."},{"claim_ids":["clm_59095687ee138fad352c490296857b5e896f06afb72f7c4e76a90aac547e4af2"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The review command accepts a PR ID, full PR URL, branch name, or default local changes, plus a --project flag for whole-project review and an -a flag to run a single agent."}],"claim_ids":["clm_1d4e64be3035c748c818e5eb328fc24029a5ad988b2d3c15da08e98704e505d1","clm_2282cc45b7b763672a60bffcde8e090ecb761c78a0c2ab299357fea5fffa4fcf","clm_59095687ee138fad352c490296857b5e896f06afb72f7c4e76a90aac547e4af2"],"created_at":"2026-09-14T03:15:54Z","created_by_operation":"op_0dc34ece6c474b6d84cb523f4888da66","id":"pg_a7eeae5c99485aa19ab133fa53b4bfdd","maturity":"draft","page_type":"source","path":"pages/sources/strategic-automation-dspy-compounding-engineering-docs-api-config-md-9-33fa53b4bfdd.md","record_type":"page","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","source_ids":["src_619f78a00dd056cda58342de935dc75f"],"title":"Strategic-Automation/dspy-compounding-engineering/docs/api/config.md @ 918f63caff79","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:15:54Z","updated_by_operation":"op_0dc34ece6c474b6d84cb523f4888da66"}
